<title>USA: Haiti, Jamaica offered US export credits for feed.</title>
<headline>Haiti, Jamaica offered US export credits for feed.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said Wednesday it added animal feed products to the list of items eligible for export credit guarantees on sales to Haiti and Jamaica.</p>
<p>Total fiscal 1997 credits to the West Caribbean region, consisting of the two nations, remained at $40 million, USDA said. Credits were offered through the short-term GSM-102 program.</p>
<p>Animal feed products include protein supplements of animal or vegetable origin, compound feed, animal milk replacer and calf starter pre-mix, USDA said.</p>
</text>
